<Figures layout="steps">
	<OriginStep bind:t step="name">It begins with a name, and the + of its C++, the language llama.cpp is written in.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="plus">A plus with the icon’s own arms: 240 wide upright, {lower} deep across.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="l">Keep the top arm, the centre and the right arm: an L inside the +.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="open">Lift out the centre block the + and the L share. Stem and foot now touch at one point.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="lean">In a flash the bolt leans it: the L slants 30° on the baseline, every edge at {deg}°, with the bolt inside.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="soften">Round only the two outer corners. That is the Llama icon.</OriginStep>
</Figures>

